  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "Enhance the Text objects by adding get/set_antialiased methods. Currently, Text objects always retrieve their antialiasing state via the global rcParams['text.antialias'], unlike other artists that support per-artist configuration. The solution is to add similar getters and setters on Text objects \u2013 and adjust Annotations accordingly \u2013 so that the antialiased property can be individually set and retrieved. This change will allow users to control antialiasing on a per-instance basis rather than relying solely on the global setting.",
    "hint_texts": "This feature involves modifying the Text class (and its Annotation subclass) in lib/matplotlib/text.py. Developers should add an instance attribute (e.g., _antialiased) initialized from rcParams and create set_antialiased and get_antialiased methods. The implementation must ensure that when the antialiased property is updated, any necessary flags (e.g., stale) are set to trigger a re-render. Review the constructor (__init__) and the _reset_visual_defaults method to integrate the new parameter and guarantee that Annotation objects mirror these changes.",
    "entrypoint": "File: lib/matplotlib/text.py. Focus on the Text class constructor (__init__), the _reset_visual_defaults method, and the new methods set_antialiased and get_antialiased. Also verify that changes propagate correctly to the Annotation subclass.",
