  "feature2": {
    "prompt": "Adjust the backend rendering code to utilize the new antialiased property. At present, backends such as the agg and cairo modules rely on the global rcParams['text.antialiased'] setting when drawing text. The solution is to replace these global accesses with calls to the GraphicsContext\u2019s get_antialiased() method so that the drawing stage respects the per-artist antialiasing settings provided by Text objects and Annotations. This will ensure rendering behavior is consistent with the new configurable antialiasing API.",
    "hint_texts": "This feature focuses on the drawing backends. Developers should modify lib/matplotlib/backends/backend_agg.py and lib/matplotlib/backends/backend_cairo.py. Find the sections in the draw_text functions where antialiasing is set \u2013 for example, look for references to mpl.rcParams['text.antialiased'] \u2013 and replace them with gc.get_antialiased(). In backend_cairo.py, update the font options so that opts.set_antialias() uses the value from the graphics context. Also, add or update any necessary getter methods in the GraphicsContext to support this change.",
    "entrypoint": "Files to update: lib/matplotlib/backends/backend_agg.py (modify draw_text to use gc.get_antialiased()) and lib/matplotlib/backends/backend_cairo.py (modify draw_text to set antialiasing via opts.set_antialias(gc.get_antialiased()) and add a getter for antialiased if needed).",
