  "collaboration_points": {
    "shared_resources": "Both features rely on the modifications in lib/matplotlib/text.py (for the new _antialiased attribute and related methods) and on the GraphicsContext used by the rendering backends. The rcParams settings and the updated antialiased property are common resources that both parts must handle.",
    "integration_strategy": "Feature1 must be completed first to establish the new per-artist API. Feature2 then integrates this API into the backend drawing routines by replacing global settings with the new getter method. Integration testing should focus on verifying that Text objects pass the correct antialiased state to the backends.",
    "communication_needs": "Developers working on Feature1 and Feature2 should coordinate on the API design and naming conventions to ensure consistency. Regular discussions are recommended to align on how the new antialiased property gets propagated from text objects to the GraphicsContext and subsequently used by the drawing methods. Clear checkpoints and integration tests will aid in merging the two parts seamlessly."
